-## 9. Code Examples (libcurl, POSIX)
+## 9. Rate Limiting
+
+EduGate applies a per-client-IP rate limit before routing validation. The limiter first looks for a version-specific policy such as `rate_limit_v1` or `rate_limit_v2`; if none is configured for the request version, it falls back to the deprecated global default. Configure limits in `config/gateway.conf` and rebuild the gateway.
+
+```c
+static const gateway_conf_t G_GATEWAY_CONF = {
+    .rate_limit_enabled        = true,
+    .rate_limit_requests       = 100, /* default fallback */
+    .rate_limit_window_seconds = 60,  /* default fallback */
+    .rate_limit_v1             = RL(60, 60),
+    .rate_limit_v2             = RL(500, 60)
+};
+```
+
+| Key | Type | Description |
+|-----|------|-------------|
+| `rate_limit_enabled` | `true`/`false` | Enables or disables gateway-wide rate limiting. |
+| `rate_limit_v1` | `rate_limit_t` | v1-specific requests/window policy, e.g. `RL(60, 60)`. |
+| `rate_limit_v2` | `rate_limit_t` | v2-specific requests/window policy, e.g. `RL(500, 60)`. |
+| `rate_limit_requests` | integer | Deprecated default maximum per client IP when no version-specific limit exists. |
+| `rate_limit_window_seconds` | integer | Deprecated default window length when no version-specific limit exists. |
+
+When the limit is exceeded, the gateway returns **429 Too Many Requests** with a
+JSON error body. The HTTP handler also emits a `Retry-After` header matching
+`rate_limit_window_seconds`.
+
+---
+
